    "format-version": "0.1",
    "license": "MIT",
    "name": "Metagenomic Functional Analysis ",
    "readme": "# Metagenomic Functional Profiling Workflow\n\nThis workflow performs functional annotation of metagenomic data using HUMAnN to generate gene- and pathway-level functional profiles.\n---\n\n## Inputs\n- Quality-trimmed FASTQ files (paired-end)\n- Host-derived reads removed **if applicable** (only necessary when samples contain host DNA)\n- Taxonomic profile generated by MetaPhlAn\n---\n\n## Workflow Steps  \n\n### 1. Functional Annotation\n- HUMAnN  \n  - Performs nucleotide and translated search\n  - Uses MetaPhlAn taxonomy for taxon-stratified functional profiling\n  - Generates gene-family abundance and pathway-level profiles  \n\n---\n\n## Outputs\n- Gene family abundance  \n- Pathway abundance  \n- Pathway coverage\n\n---\n\n## License\nMIT\n",
    "report": {
        "markdown": "\n# Workflow Execution Report\n\n## Workflow Inputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_inputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow Outputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_outputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow\n```galaxy\nworkflow_display()\n```\n"
    },
